# rena0-attack-empty-meter — F1-3 fixture, P2-7 attack family (melee does not cost the meter)
#
# Source: NO gauge gate on a melee press. FUN_00445ee0's explicit `0 < +0x834` tests guard
# its dash and jump arms only (its lines 59/65/72/82/92/100/441/449 bind moves 0x14/0x1e/0x28
# and the +0x830 dash selector), and the one `+0x834 < 1` (line 168) is an OR term that routes
# the press into the SHOT path — it never refuses the attack. The recovered meter therefore
# gates blocking, dashes, jump and the air dash, exactly as the owner described.
#
# The port used to decline every melee press at an empty gauge. Owner report: "i cant attack
# with normal attacks when i have no stamina, this does not exist on the original game".
#
# SCOPE, so this case is not over-read: the standing refill (+40/tick) lands on the same tick,
# so the bar reads 40 here and this fixture does NOT by itself distinguish the old gate from
# the corrected rule. It pins the pilot-path OBSERVABLE (an attack is presented while the bar
# is essentially empty, and spends no meter). The gate's own load-bearing guard is
# tests/melee_admission_test.cpp case (9), which sets the gauge to 0 with no refill in play and
# failed on the restored gate before the correction.
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 300
collision open-field
# The standing refill (+40/tick, executor case 0) lands on the same tick, so the meter reads
# 40 rather than 0 by the time the tick is observed; that is still an essentially empty bar.
charge_gauge 0
input 0 MELEE
expect 0 charge_gauge 40
expect 2 anim_row 300
